@model WebRecomp.Web.Services.SmartIntelligence.IntelligencePage
@using System.Text.Json
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Smart Intelligence";
    var r = Model.Report;
}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/smart-intelligence.css" asp-append-version="true" />
<div class="si" id="smart-intelligence" data-ai-ready="@Model.OpenAiReady.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()">
    <header class="si-heading"><div><p class="si-eyebrow">12WR / UNDERSTAND YOUR RESPONSE</p><h1>Smart Intelligence</h1><p class="si-lead">Find the underlying direction. Explore what moves together. Put the daily noise in context.</p></div><span class="si-badge">Analysis workspace · v1</span></header>
    <form method="get" class="si-toolbar" aria-label="Analysis window">
        <label>History<select name="days"><option value="42" selected="@(r.Days.Count == 42)">Last 6 weeks</option><option value="84" selected="@(r.Days.Count == 84)">Last 12 weeks</option><option value="168" selected="@(r.Days.Count == 168)">Last 24 weeks</option></select></label>
        <label>Trend response<select name="sensitivity"><option value="balanced" selected="@(r.Sensitivity == "balanced")">Balanced</option><option value="steady" selected="@(r.Sensitivity == "steady")">Steadier</option><option value="responsive" selected="@(r.Sensitivity == "responsive")">More responsive</option></select></label>
        <button class="button" type="submit">Update analysis</button><span>@r.Start.ToString("MMM d")–@r.End.ToString("MMM d, yyyy")</span>
    </form>
    <p class="si-notice">These are estimates from your existing records. Smoothing reduces daily noise; it does not establish exact tissue changes. This page does not change your food targets, workouts, or saved measurements.</p>
    <div class="si-stats" id="si-stats" aria-live="polite"></div>
    <section class="si-panel" aria-labelledby="si-trends-title">
        <div class="si-section-heading"><div><p class="si-eyebrow">01 / UNDERLYING STATES</p><h2 id="si-trends-title">The direction beneath the readings</h2></div><label class="si-check"><input id="si-averages" type="checkbox" /> Compare 3- and 7-day averages</label></div>
        <p>Solid line: causal state-space estimate. Dots: original readings. Shading: conditional model uncertainty; unknown scale bias is not included. Ordinary gaps are predicted through and become less certain.</p>
        <div class="si-chart-grid" id="si-charts"></div>
        <details class="si-details"><summary>How the trend model works</summary><p>Each series has a slowly changing level and slope. New readings update those states; unusually large residuals get less influence. Missing days predict forward without inventing a measurement. Twenty-eight earlier calendar days initialize the filters where records exist. A genuine reversal can emerge when repeated evidence supports it.</p><p>Fat, muscle, weight and water are filtered separately. We do not infer a unique fluid/tissue split from correlated scale outputs. Water is an impedance-derived estimate, and muscle includes water. Sensitivity choices change smoothing assumptions; they do not discover new facts.</p><div class="si-table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Series</th><th>Observation noise (lb)</th><th>Daily level process variance</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach(var state in r.States){<tr><td>@state.Label</td><td>@state.ObservationNoise.ToString("0.000")</td><td>@state.ProcessNoise.ToString("0.000000")</td></tr>}</tbody></table></div><p>Parameters use robust variability in the available history plus explicit noise floors. Bands and smoothing assumptions are exploratory, not clinically validated accuracy claims.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="si-panel" aria-labelledby="si-evidence-title"><p class="si-eyebrow">02 / WHAT THE RECORDS SUPPORT</p><h2 id="si-evidence-title">Evidence before explanations</h2><div class="si-findings">@foreach(var finding in r.Findings){<article><h3>@finding.Title</h3><p>@finding.Evidence</p><p class="si-muted">@finding.Interpretation</p></article>}</div></section>
    <section class="si-panel" aria-labelledby="si-correlations-title"><p class="si-eyebrow">03 / RELATIONSHIPS &amp; DELAYS</p><h2 id="si-correlations-title">What correlates—and what doesn’t</h2><p>Test the same day and one-to-three-day delays. Changes are used where appropriate to reduce shared-trend effects. Correlations are exploratory: small samples, repeated testing and serial dependence can produce misleading associations. A weak result is useful too.</p><div class="si-table-wrap"><table class="si-correlations"><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Delay</th><th>Paired days</th><th>Correlation r</th><th>Assessment</th></tr></thead><tbody>@foreach(var c in r.Correlations){<tr><td>@c.Input<small>@c.Transform</small></td><td>@c.Outcome</td><td>@c.LagDays day(s)</td><td>@c.Pairs</td><td><span class="si-r">@(c.R?.ToString("+0.00;-0.00;0.00") ?? "—")</span></td><td>@c.Status</td></tr>}</tbody></table></div><p class="si-muted">No association here establishes that a food caused fat gain, that a craving diagnosed a deficiency, or that a water change corrected the muscle estimate.</p></section>
    <section class="si-panel" aria-labelledby="si-week-title"><p class="si-eyebrow">04 / FUEL, TRAINING &amp; RECOVERY</p><h2 id="si-week-title">The weeks around the changes</h2><div class="si-week-grid">@foreach(var week in r.WeeklySummaries){<article><h3>@week.Title</h3><p>@week.Evidence</p><p class="si-muted">@week.Interpretation</p></article>}</div><p>Targets come from captured same-day prescriptions where available, otherwise the latest stored recommendation. Missing targets stay unknown; this workspace does not rerun the engine or manufacture historical prescriptions. The daily evidence below identifies the source.</p></section>
    <section class="si-panel si-ai" aria-labelledby="si-ai-title"><div class="si-section-heading"><div><p class="si-eyebrow">05 / CONNECT THE EVIDENCE</p><h2 id="si-ai-title">OpenAI analysis</h2></div><span class="si-badge">@(Model.OpenAiReady ? "Connection configured" : "Connection needed") · @Model.OpenAiModel</span></div><p>Review the trends, preceding nutrition, completed training, sleep and energy together. Findings distinguish observations from hypotheses and cite dates. Analysis stays advisory.</p>
        <form id="si-ai-form" method="post" action="/SmartIntelligence/Analyze">@Html.AntiForgeryToken()<label for="si-context">Anything the logs don’t capture? <span class="si-muted">Optional</span></label><textarea id="si-context" name="context" maxlength="1500" rows="3" placeholder="For example: fatigue, brain fog, travel, changes in appetite, or eating extra to meet a target."></textarea><label class="si-check"><input type="checkbox" id="si-include-notes" checked /> Include saved recovery, food and exercise notes</label><p class="si-muted">Running analysis sends this window’s dates, readings, nutrition, completed training, check-ins and your added context to OpenAI. Names, email addresses and account IDs are excluded. Saved notes are included only if selected.</p><button class="button" type="submit" id="si-analyze" disabled="@(!Model.OpenAiReady)">Analyze with OpenAI</button><p id="si-ai-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">@(Model.OpenAiReady ? "Ready to analyze your current evidence." : "Trends and correlations are ready. An administrator can enable OpenAI in Admin → Manage Connections.")</p></form>
        <div id="si-ai-result" aria-live="polite"></div>
        @if(Model.IsAdmin){<p><a asp-controller="AdminExternalConnections" asp-action="Index" asp-fragment="openai">Manage OpenAI connection in Admin → Manage Connections</a></p>}
        <p class="si-muted">Provider interface: OpenAI is available first. Additional analysis providers can use the same evidence and versioned model output later.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="si-panel"><details><summary>Daily evidence &amp; model diagnostics</summary><p>Current-day food is unfinished and excluded from completed-day comparisons. Totals below 1,000 calories are flagged as possibly partial, not proven incomplete. Missing workouts are unknown, not assumed rest.</p><button type="button" class="button" id="si-export">Download analysis JSON</button><div class="si-table-wrap" id="si-daily"></div><h3>Completed workout details</h3><div id="si-workouts"></div></details></section>
    <footer class="si-footer">@r.Version · Evidence fingerprint @r.Fingerprint[..12] · Read-only analysis</footer>
    <script id="si-data" type="application/json">@Html.Raw(JsonSerializer.Serialize(r,new JsonSerializerOptions(JsonSerializerDefaults.Web)))</script>
</div>
<script src="~/js/smart-intelligence.js" asp-append-version="true" defer></script>
